-* **Strengths**: Joint optimization of geometry and appearance; flexible topology updates; differentiable rendering allows gradient-based optimization from 2D cues [S1, unofficial].
-* **Limitations**: Computationally expensive due to repeated tetrahedralization and marching tetrahedra; sensitive to initialization and hyperparameters (e.g., `accumulation_delaunay`); requires multi-view inputs [S1, unofficial].
